WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.960
What looks like an alien spaceship—

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.630
Is actually a tiny object made up of an air pocket

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.190
surrounding a metal ball--plunging through liquid.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.210
The air pocket creates a nearly frictionless surface

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.150
and is falling at a constant velocity.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.150
Normally, a solid moving in liquid is slowed down

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.750
by friction and drag.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.849
So, how did researchers reduce drag to nearly zero?

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:24.660
By creating a nonwetting surface

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.620
using one of two approaches:

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.240
Heating up a metal ball so hot that what’s called

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.420
a Leidenfrost effect occurs--

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.520
where a vapor layer forms

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.200
between the ball and the liquid.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.660
Like water beading on a hot stove.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.880
Or coating the metal ball with a hydrophobic

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.480
or super water repellent substance.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.340
The balls are then placed at specific heights

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.580
above a deep tank.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.980
Here, a 20mm steel ball preheated to

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.920
400 °C is dropped at a height of

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.770
55 cm into 95°C water.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.360
At impact, an air pocket forms.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.420
It stabilizes into a streamlined shape by shedding

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.180
small air bubbles at the tail

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.860
until it achieves a constant velocity.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.940
The dropped hydrophobic ball also forms an air pocket

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.800
and at similar velocities,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.560
without the need of pre-heating the ball or fluid.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.600
Previous drag reduction schemes

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.440
have also used air pockets-

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.460
but a very thin layer around the object,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.130
so they basically retained their original shape.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.280
In contrast, the present methods rely on creating

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.440
a very large, tear shaped air pocket—

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.620
from 5 to 15 times the volume of the balls themselves—

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.580
changing the solid sphere into a giant air torpedo.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.800
To determine if drag has been reduced,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.620
researchers then raced the air pocket balls

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.360
against plastic projectiles

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.360
with matching weights and shapes.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.000
Analyzing the high speed footage,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.740
they found drag was reduced by 90%

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.840
compared to the plastic dummies.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.160
Predicting the movement of bodies in fluids

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.580
is usually difficult because of resisting forces

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.400
but since these new methods

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.850
virtually eliminate friction and turbulence,

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.290
velocities can be accurately calculated based on

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.420
the density of the ball and the volume of the air pocket.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.920
Next, researchers want to nail down exactly

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.900
how the shapes of the air pockets are determined.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.740
Since these objects require

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.160
so little energy to travel through water--

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.200
perhaps these methods could be applied

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.460
to energy efficient, high speed transportation

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.500
in the future.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.840
Engineers already are releasing bubbles under ships

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.750
to reduce fuel costs.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.630
Maybe shaping those bubbles or using them

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:32.300
with hydrophobic coating could speed things along.

